Sure! To update a break node’s label to `'loopEnd'`, you’ll need to pass the node (in string form) and the new label to the `updateBreak` function. Here’s how you can do it:

```javascript
const result = await functions.updateBreak({
  node: /* your break node as a string */,
  label: "loopEnd"
});
```

If the node already has the label `'loopEnd'`, the function will simply return the node unchanged. Let me know if you’d like help formatting the node or if you have any other questions!
